<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Postbank - 1996 loss after special transfer.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Postbank - 1996 loss after special transfer.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Postbank AG said on Monday it made a net loss of 1.256 billion marks in 1996 after the deduction of a special transfer to reserves for its cooperation with Germany's Post AG.</p>
<p>The figure compares with a 226 million mark profit for 1995.</p>
<p>Postbank also reported a profit of 308 million marks after regular loan loss provisions. For 1995, it reported a profit of 234 million marks after a routine transfer of profits to the Bonn federal government.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
